   "html_text": "Generally speaking, there are five potential replies to this argument. First, one could accept (4) and admit that David is not identical to Lump. We consider this idea in sections 2 and 3, when we discuss the constitution view of David Wiggins (1968) and the temporal parts theory of David Lewis (1976). Second, one could deny (1) by either rejecting the existence of David or by insisting that David existed on Monday. We examine these approaches in section 4, where we review the eliminativist view",
   "md_text": "Generally speaking, there are five potential replies to this argument. First, one could accept (4) and admit that David is not identical to Lump. We consider this idea in sections 2 and 3, when we discuss the constitution view of David Wiggins (1968) and the temporal parts theory of David Lewis (1976). Second, one could deny (1) by either rejecting the existence of David or by insisting that David existed on Monday. We examine these approaches in section 4, where we review the eliminativist view"
